## 5. UX / Design Rationale (breakdown)

| Aspect | Decision |
|---|---|
| Placement | Toolbar, right after the Board/Gantt switch — it belongs to “how the board is rendered”, not to board administration. |
| States | Active mode is `btn-ghost` + `text-primary` + check-styled active item; menu items show label + one-line description (`whitespace-normal`) so the behaviour is discoverable without docs. |
| Accessibility | `role="button"`, `aria-label`, `aria-pressed`, `title` carrying label + description; keyboard reachable via daisyUI `dropdown` (`tabindex="0"`). |
| Defaults | Sprint → `attention` (no data = identical to today's `updated_at` order). Kanban → `manual` (keeps column `chats` order). Zero silent regressions. |
| PM-tool contract | `pinned` (hard top), `priority` high/medium/low, `sort_index` — all already persisted by the backend `Chat` model, set via `/api/chats/metadata`. |

**Anti-patterns avoided**
- No new chat field / no backend migration: ordering reuses persisted fields, so tools and UI share one contract.
- No cloning of chats in getters (would break card identity and re-render the board on every chat write).
- No per-column order override: one board-level setting avoids N conflicting switches.

**Iteration guideline**
1. Load a sprint with mixed tasks → verify nothing moves (no ordering data yet).
2. Let the PM tools (or the task dialog) set `priority: 'high'` on a blocked task → it jumps to the top of its column.
3. Switch to `Manual`, drag a card → order persists after reload (`sort_index`).
4. Switch to `Last updated` → confirm the previous behaviour is still reachable.

